{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Declared mutants of v8-engine-io-user-files (docs/architecture/io.md, \"User files\"). Run with docs/architecture/plans/time-threads-trace/scripts/run_mutations.py --catalog docs/architecture/plans/framework-rework/scripts/io_user_files_mutations.json --build-dir <a tree with BUILD_TESTING=ON>. io-within-case runs on Windows only (SamePathComponent ignores case there); io-within-lexical-dot-dot on macOS and Linux only (on Windows MakeAbsolute already removes '..' as written, as the OS does). The explicit regular-file check in ProbeFileStamp has no mutant: engine/os refuses the same paths with the same code and message when opening, so only the side effects of opening (a pipe, a device) tell them apart. A mutant is killed only when its check fails with the expected message.",
  "mutants": [
    {
      "id": "io-within-any-name",
      "what": "Containment ignores the names it compares, so a sibling with a longer name counts as inside",
      "file": "engine/io/src/fs/NativeFileSystem.cpp",
      "find": "            if (candidatePart == candidate.end() || !SameComponent(*candidatePart, *rootPart)) return false;",
      "replace": "            if (candidatePart == candidate.end()) return false;",
      "target": "engine_tests",
      "cases": "*ProbeFileStamp*,*WriteFileAtomically creates*,*IsNativePathWithin*",
      "expect": "is NOT correct"
    },
    {
      "id": "io-within-case",
      "what": "Names are compared byte for byte instead of by the platform rule",
      "file": "engine/io/src/fs/NativeFileSystem.cpp",
      "find": "            auto same = Os::Files::SamePathComponent(leftText.value(), rightText.value());\n            return same && same.value();",
      "replace": "            return leftText.value() == rightText.value();",
      "target": "engine_tests",
      "cases": "*ProbeFileStamp*,*WriteFileAtomically creates*,*IsNativePathWithin*",
      "expect": "is NOT correct",
      "platforms": [
        "win32"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "io-stamp-missing-is-error",
      "what": "A missing file is an error instead of exists == false",
      "file": "engine/io/src/helpers/UserFiles.cpp",
